---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="For sellers"
  description="What a Verdict flag means, and how to dispute one."
>
  <h1>If Verdict flagged your listing</h1>
  <p>
    Verdict measures patterns in review data. The name describes what the tool outputs, not a
    legal finding against you or your business. It does not say you did anything, and it does
    not accuse you of anything. A flag means the reviews on the listing are distributed in a
    way that resembles listings where reviews were solicited.
  </p>
  <p>
    There are honest reasons this happens. A viral moment. A large influencer campaign. A
    reused listing from a product you sold previously.
  </p>
  <p>
    Send us the listing and what you think we got wrong. We will re run it, explain each
    signal and its number, and if the analysis is wrong we will say so publicly on the
    <a href="/status">status page</a> and use it to improve the model.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="button-secondary" href="mailto:sellers@verdict.tools">Contact us about a listing</a>
  </p>
</Layout>
